Hunk positions refreshed for libpsl 0.23.3; no code changes.

From f4b9035a06eb95a01f4b3419dfbcf3226d1122b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Radhika <radhika@research.itecz.au>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:12:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] is_public_suffix: also look up the IDNA ACE form of a
 non-ASCII domain

With builtin data, a text PSL or a UTF-8 DAFSA the lookup compared the
raw UTF-8 bytes only, so a domain that the IDNA mapping changes never
matched, e.g. "xxx.\xC2\xADck" (soft hyphen U+00AD, which UTS46 and
nameprep drop) is xxx.ck under the *.ck rule, but
psl_is_public_suffix(psl_builtin(), ...) returned 0 and
psl_is_cookie_domain_acceptable() accepted a cookie for it.

Move the DAFSA/vector lookup into lookup_suffix(), try the domain as
given first and, if that misses and the domain is non-ASCII, the ACE
form from the IDNA runtime. Builtin and UTF-8 data contain the ACE form
of every rule, so this finds the same entries. ASCII DAFSA results are
unchanged, the conversion just happens after the miss instead of before.
